\section{Other models, including BioCLIP}{

Any open_clip model whose image side is a vision transformer works. The
key builders only see its embeddings, so nothing else changes.
\itemize{
\item \code{visionModel(name = "bioclip")} loads
\href{https://imageomics.github.io/bioclip/}{BioCLIP} and
\code{visionModel(name = "bioclip-2")} BioCLIP 2, models trained on images of
organisms, from the Hugging Face Hub. They are downloaded on first use.
\item \code{name = "hf-hub:<organisation>/<model>"} loads any other open_clip model
on the Hub, and \code{name = "local-dir:<folder>"} a copy you have downloaded
(the folder holds the model's \code{open_clip_config.json} and weights file).
\item \code{name} and \code{pretrained} together select one of open_clip's built-in
models, e.g. \verb{name = "ViT-B-16", pretrained = "laion2b_s34b_b88k"}.
}

A key can only be followed with the model it was built with: use the same
model for \code{\link[=embedImages]{embedImages()}} and later for \code{\link[=scoreImages]{scoreImages()}}.

BioCLIP's text side was trained on names of organisms, not on descriptions
of what they look like. It suits sniglets (\code{\link[=discoverSniglets]{discoverSniglets()}}), which use
images only, better than vocabulary questions (\code{\link[=keyFromClusters]{keyFromClusters()}}).
}

